to shared_live, to republish safely. Title, favicon, icon and contract need no echo: omit them on publish_version to keep the values returned here.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"slug": {"description": "The artifact's slug (UUID) or claude.ai link.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["slug"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__get_artifact"}, "server": "claude-artifacts"}, {"description": "How to write and publish an artifact page with this server: fixed guidance, by topic. Read the pages topic before the first publish of a session, the design topic before writing or restyling a page, and the diagrams topic before drawing a diagram in a page. With no topic it lists the topics.", "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__guide", "schema": {"description": "How to write and publish an artifact page with this server: fixed guidance, by topic. Read the pages topic before the first publish of a session, the design topic before writing or restyling a page, and the diagrams topic before drawing a diagram in a page. With no topic it lists the topics.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"topic": {"description": "The topic to read. Omit to list the topics.", "enum": ["pages", "design", "editorial", "diagrams"], "type": "string"}}, "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__guide"}, "server": "claude-artifacts"}, {"description": "List artifacts in your organization that you can open: your own, then those shared with you or that you have viewed, most recent first; with shared_only, only the latter. Each entry carries slug, title, favicon, description, the version id you are served (pass it as base_version only for artifacts you own or can edit), whether it is yours ('mine') or 'shared', when it last changed (your own only), and its claude.ai URL. soft_deleted: true marks one of your own that was deleted or taken down: only you see it listed, and republishing it is refused. Titles and descriptions of sha