 person supplied it, and whatever purpose is claimed, such as a prop or a test, when the page would work as the real thing. If publishing is refused, Claude does not suggest other ways to host or share the page.", "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__publish_files", "schema": {"description": "Publish an artifact from files on disk: their bytes do not pass through you. Prefer this to publish_version when the page's files already exist, when there is more than one file or an image, or when the page is large. For each file give `as`, the path it is served at, and `path`, its absolute path on the machine where your own file tools run; leave `uri` out. index.html is required in a new artifact. Limits for one call: 256 files, 20 MiB a file, 64 MiB in all. The client may refuse a file it will not send, such as a secrets file, a link or a path outside the working folder. Omit slug to create an artifact, private to you. To republish, give slug and base_version (from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish); title and icon are kept when omitted. Past 256 files, send the rest in later republishes. A republish changes only the files named and keeps the rest, which stay served: to take a file away, list it in remove. mode \"replace\" removes the artifact's own files that are not named. This tool publishes only to an artifact of yours. **Files Claude did not write**: Claude reads the whole file before publishing it, even when the person asks it not to. Publishing distributes the content, and Claude never distributes what it has not seen. A request for privacy is a reason to read before publishing, not an exemption. If Claude cannot read the file, it does not publish it. **Claude never publishes** a page that impersonates a real person or organization, for example by using their name, branding, byline or domain. Claude also never publishes fabricated records, receipts or reviews presented as genuine, forms or flows that collect credentials or payment details under false pretenses, or content that targets a private individual. Claude refuses whether it wrote the page or the person supplied it, and whatever purpose is claimed, such as a prop or a test, when the page would work as the real thing. If publishing is refused, Claude does not suggest other ways to host or share the page.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"artifact_title": {"description": "The artifact's current title, as get_artifact gives it. Needed when shared_live is 'public'.", "type": "string"}, "base_version": {"description": "Required when republishing: the version this publish replaces.", "type": "string"}, "contract": {"description": "Optional runtime-contract version. Leave it out to keep the current one.", "type": "string"}, "files": {"description": "Before this tool changes an artifact that exists, call list_files: a file already there keeps its path in that list, every folder included, as its `as`. Skip the call only if you have just created the artifact, or if that list or an earlier publish_files call on it is itself in this conversation (a summary does not count). If list_files refuses, go on with the paths you have, unless its answer says to retry, to send no files, or that publishing changes nothing.", "items": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"as": {"description": "The path the file is served at, e.g. index.html or css/site.css. Give every folder. In an artifact made from a type, put a new file under the top folder of the type's content.index, unless the type's instructions place it elsewhere. Its extension says what it is served as.", "type": "string"}, "path": {"description": "Give this: the file's absolute path on the machine where your own file tools run.", "type": "string"}, "uri": {"description": "Leave out: the client fills it in.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["as"], "type": "object"}, "maxItems": 256, "type": "array"}, "icon": {"description": "One short, generic word for the tab icon. Pass one when creating.", "type": "string"}, "label": {"description": "Optional short version label.", "type": "string"}, "mode": {"description": "For a republish; leave it out when creating. patch (default): only the files named change. replace: the files named become the artifact's own files, and any other file of its own is removed. A file that comes from the artifact's type or from another artifact is not the artifact's own, and it stays when the call leaves it out.", "type": "string"}, "remove": {"description": "For a republish: served paths to delete, spelled as list_files gives them. A path the artifact does not hold is ignored without an error. To delete and change nothing else, give files as an empty list.", "items": {"type": "string"}, "maxItems": 256, "type": "array"}, "shared_live": {"description": "States who the artifact you are republishing is already shared with, and changes nothing: its 'read' value from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result. Required when that value is 'users' (named people or groups), 'org' (the user's whole organization) or 'public' (anyone with the link). Leave it out for a new artifact and when the value is 'owner'. Rejected if it does not match the artifact's current value.", "type": "string"}, "slug": {"description": "The artifact's slug. Omit to create a new artifact.", "type": "string"}, "title": {"description": "Browser-tab title. Required when creating.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["files"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__publish_files"}, "server": "claude-artifacts"}, {"description": "Publish an artifact: either create a new artifact — omit slug and give title and content; you become its owner and it starts private to you — or publish a new version of an artifact you own, or of one in your organization that you can edit — give slug and base_version. Some clients may publish only to your own artifacts: there the call is refused as owner-only. Republishing is read-then-send: base_version must name the live version you are replacing (from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result) — if it is no longer live, the publish is rejected with a conflict; re-read and retry from the current state. On success the new version goes live immediately. When republishing, the artifact's stored connectors manifest carries forward unchanged, and so do title, favicon, icon and contract when omitted. Content is capped at 16 MiB.", "name": "mcp__claude-artifacts__publish_version", "schema": {"description": "Publish an artifact: either create a new artifact — omit slug and give title and content; you become its owner and it starts private to you — or publish a new version of an artifact you own, or of one in your organization that you can edit — give slug and base_version. Some clients may publish only to your own artifacts: there the call is refused as owner-only. Republishing is read-then-send: base_version must name the live version you are replacing (from get_artifact, read_artifact or your last publish result) — if it is no longer live, the publish is rejected with a conflict; re-read and retry from the current state. On success the new version goes live immediately. When republishing, the artifact's stored connectors manifest carries forward unchanged, and so do title, favicon, icon and contract when omitted. Content is capped at 16 MiB.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"artifact_title": {"description": "The artifact's current title, as get_artifact gives it. Needed when shared_live is 'public'.", "type": "string"}, "base_version": {"description": "Required when slug is given: the version id this publish replaces — echo the version get_artifact or read_artifact returned (or your last publish result's). Rejected with a conflict if it no longer names the live version, so concurrent edits are never silently overwritten. Omit when creating.", "type": "string"}, "content": {"description": "The complete H