se-insensitive substring matched against full_name (owner/repo). Empty matches everything.", "type": "string"}}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_repos"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "List Claude Code Remote sessions visible to the authenticated account. In bot contexts (e.g. Slack) this is a shared pool spanning many people, not just the human asking — pass mine: true to narrow to sessions started by the same account as the calling session. Returns session IDs, titles, statuses, and timestamps. status_bucket is the board bucket (working / blocked / review_ready / completed / failed) — read this for \"running / waiting on you / done / errored\"; updated_at is the last event. Where shown, a row also has parent_session_id, task_summary and post_turn_summary (recent_action, needs_action). To read how a session's last turn ended, call list_events with kinds [\"result\"] and limit 100.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__list_sessions", "schema": {"description": "List Claude Code Remote sessions visible to the authenticated account. In bot contexts (e.g. Slack) this is a shared pool spanning many people, not just the human asking — pass mine: true to narrow to sessions started by the same account as the calling session. Returns session IDs, titles, statuses, and timestamps. status_bucket is the board bucket (working / blocked / review_ready / completed / failed) — read this for \"running / waiting on you / done / errored\"; updated_at is the last event. Where shown, a row also has parent_session_id, task_summary and post_turn_summary (recent_action, needs_action). To read how a session's last turn ended, call list_events with kinds [\"result\"] and limit 100.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {"after_id": {"description": "Pagination cursor: return sessions older than this session ID. Pass the last_id from a previous response to get the next page.", "type": "string"}, "before_id": 