minder) delivers into that ongoing conversation, while a fresh-session scheduled task starts from nothing and needs a complete standalone instruction.", "type": "string"}, "run_once_at": {"description": "New one-shot fire time, in one of the forms that create_trigger's run_once_at takes: a local date and time and then the IANA zone name in brackets, with no UTC offset (e.g. 2026-04-20T09:00:00[America/Los_Angeles]), or an RFC3339 timestamp (e.g. 2026-04-20T17:00:00Z). Must be in the future. Setting this clears cron_expression (and any ended_reason). Use exactly the time asked: the guidance on recurring schedules does not apply to a one-time run.", "type": "string"}, "trigger_id": {"description": "The scheduled task's trigger ID to update (starts with 'trig_'). Returned by create_trigger or list_triggers.", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["trigger_id"], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__update_trigger"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}, {"description": "Create an inbound webhook for this session and return its URL plus a sealed credential. Hand both to the artifact service's subscribe endpoint; when that service POSTs to the URL, the request body is delivered into this conversation as a <webhook-payload> message and wakes the session if idle. The signing secret inside sealed_secret is encrypted to the artifact service — it cannot be read, used, or leaked from this conversation, and only the artifact service can sign deliveries with it. A watch ends when the session ends, so call watch_url again after resuming to get a fresh one. Use this when asked to be notified when something external changes (for example, a subscribed artifact is republished). To stop, call unwatch_url with the returned trigger_id.", "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__watch_url", "schema": {"description": "Create an inbound webhook for this session and return its URL plus a sealed credential. Hand both to the artifact service's subscribe endpoint; when that service POSTs to the URL, the request body is delivered into this conversation as a <webhook-payload> message and wakes the session if idle. The signing secret inside sealed_secret is encrypted to the artifact service — it cannot be read, used, or leaked from this conversation, and only the artifact service can sign deliveries with it. A watch ends when the session ends, so call watch_url again after resuming to get a fresh one. Use this when asked to be notified when something external changes (for example, a subscribed artifact is republished). To stop, call unwatch_url with the returned trigger_id.", "eager_input_streaming": true, "input_schema": {"properties": {}, "required": [], "type": "object"}, "name": "mcp__claude-code-remote__watch_url"}, "server": "claude-code-remote"}], "type": "prompt_snapshot"}, "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "claude/rainbow-3d-recovery-m4v347", "isSidechain": true, "parentUuid": "c11a06ff-3ab4-415b-9156-98a921420ca3", "sessionId": "e0f002d9-e93b-5e8f-89ac-1e3fceebb58f", "timestamp": "2026-11-15T18:37:00.864Z", "type": "attachment", "userType": "external", "uuid": "505d9a83-3899-4049-901e-9499954007d2", "version": "2.1.325"}
