{"agentId": "a9ee02bd616f45378", "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "claude/rainbow-3d-recovery-m4v347", "isSidechain": true, "message": {"content": [{"content": "1\t# RAINBOW — NEW 11-SCREEN CLAUDE CODE MASTER BUILD PROMPT\n2\t\n3\t**MANDATE: BUILD A BRAND-NEW RAINBOW GAME FROM THESE EXACT APPROVED REFERENCES.** This is a new isolated project. Do not modify, copy, fork, overwrite, or reuse repositories, assets, models, scenes, characters, code, or branches from Bubble Wash Kingdom, Ripple, bubblegames, or any other earlier project. The only approved source files are the 11 image references and official new cartoon-girl reference shipped in THIS package.\n4\t\n5\t**Project title:** RAINBOW. **Proposed private GitHub repo:** `rainbow-washer-game` (use this name if available; if it exists, DO NOT overwrite or clone old content; report the collision and use an explicitly confirmed new name). Verify any new remote, default branch, first commit SHA and push, and tell me what was actually created. If no GitHub access exists, keep working locally and clearly report the authentication blocker rather than claiming a push.\n6\t\n7\t## 0. FIRST ACTION: READ THE SOURCES AND KEEP THEM IMMUTABLE\n8\t\n9\tRead `README_FIRST.md`, `REFERENCE_ORDER.md`, `character_references/official_cartoon_girl_original.jpg`, and *all eleven* files in `references/` at full resolution BEFORE designing anything. These images are locked targets, NOT broad inspiration. Preserve the originals byte-for-byte. Check the SHA-256 list and native dimensions in `REFERENCE_ORDER.md`. There is no 12th stage.\n10\t\n11\tThe new official cartoon girl is a **mandatory, narrowly scoped visual override** of the previously pictured human characters. Use HER in the opening, when the girl is visible behind the door in Scene 10, and in the real final Scene 11. **The girl visible in the uploaded Scene 11 image is NOT the identity to model; it is a reference for composition, towel, environment and final UI only.** Do not mix their heads, outfits, hairstyles or proportions. Keep Benny unchanged. Everything else in 01–11 stays as close to the original reference as a real-time 3D build allows.\n12\t\n13\t**Hard rule:** deliver a real controllable 3D game on Android, not a slide show, static screenshot, video, skybox, wallpaper or pre-rendered film being presented as gameplay. The cinematic start and victory ending may use real-time cutscenes, but the ride itself must run on 3D geometry with steering/swimming, coin collection, moving water and camera/path continuity.\n14\t\n15\t## 1. OFFICIAL CHARACTERS — DO NOT REDESIGN\n16\t\n17\t**Benny:** ONE reusable, rigged 3D version of the exact pink fluffy round mascot from the source photos. Retain soft pink fur, proportions, violet eyes, rosy cheeks, little paw pads, purple-and-white ribbed/knitted beanie with a big deep-purple pom-pom and gold star on the side. He is cute, alive, reactive, able to kick/swim/paddle, tumble and ride currents. Do not replace him with another pink creature; use the SAME geometry, materials, fur style, rig, hat and star in front/rear views through ALL scenes. Rear camera on travel stages, not head-on. Benny is never seen by the girl.\n18\t\n19\t**Official cartoon girl, overriding the old girls:** One and only ONE rigged girl model based on `character_references/official_cartoon_girl_original.jpg`. Her distinctive silhouette is curly dark/warm-brown high ponytail, purple headband tied into a big purple bow with a small gold/yellow star, large cartoon eyes, friendly rounded face, warm smile, gold hoop earrings, lavender-and-white horizontally striped hoodie with gold star on sleeve, blue jeans with cuffed legs and prominent star-patch pocket, purple/white sneakers with yellow star details. Maintain the same facial proportions, hair silhouette, costume, colors, materials, age-neutral childlike cartoon proportions and art direction across all appearances. The high-quality, soft, warm, colorful 3D animated look must suit Benny. **Avoid photorealistic faces, lifelike skin, semi-realistic women, or a different-looking girl in Scene 11.** Make her recognizable even from behind or seen through glass. A single front/side/back turntable and consistent rig are required before scene integration.\n20\t\n21\t**Opening continuity:** She sorts/handles laundry, carries or pours a load containing Benny concealed in the purple towel into the washer, closes the door, and walks away at normal human speed. Benny stays concealed until she cannot see him; if he peeks in Scene 01, she is already walking away. Her walk, hands, blinking, cloth grasp, clothing movement and towel interaction must be smooth, casual and non-robotic. Do not show her noticing Benny. This opening action may occur *before* the first locked screenshot checkpoint without introducing another numbered screen.\n22\t\n23\t**Ending continuity:** In Scene 10, same cartoon girl is visible through the washer door/window, unaware of Benny. In Scene 11, she opens the metallic door, leans in and retrieves/holds the folded purple towel from the perforated platform while Benny stays safely hidden inside it. Match the approved final shot's camera, shelf, open door, violet towel, golden trim and `FINAL SPIN COMPLETE` victory badge—but substitute the official cartoon girl, including her signature bow, striped hoodie and hair. Never change back to the more realistic girl pictured in the original Stage 11. Keep the final happy and cohesive with the introduction.\n24\t\n25\t## 2. LOCKED SCENES IN EXACT CHRONOLOGICAL ORDER\n26\t\n27\tThe numbering below corresponds directly to the original filenames and files. Do not rename stages, merge stages, insert unrelated environments or skip transitions. Match each image's shapes, colors, object placement, camera scale, framing, lighting, foam, reflections and UI.\n28\t\n29\t**01 — Inside the Washing Machine** (`01_inside_washer_girl_and_towel.png`). Cinematic without HUD. Camera INSIDE glossy perforated pink-magenta gold-rimmed drum facing the round washer opening. The **official cartoon girl** is visible walking away in the bright laundry room, purple towel conceals Benny, glossy cyan and pink waves lift floating blue-and-white sock and pink T-shirt with yellow star. Sparkly bubbles, reflective gold washers and rich texture. Intro must lead physically into Scene 02.\n30\t\n31\t**02 — Whirlpool Tumble** (`02_mascot_tumbles_in_whirlpool.png`). Same drum from a dynamic angle, liquid sweeps in a large clockwise-like swirl; Benny tumbles with spiral eyes, visible paws, purple towel, blue striped sock, pink star T-shirt. Keep her out of Benny's view. No HUD. His tumble must naturally join the funnel opening of Scene 03.\n32\t\n33\t**03 · WHIRLPOOL TWIRL** (`03_whirlpool_twirl.png`). HUD hearts 5/5, $ 1,330, pause; level strip same title. Polished cyan/hot-pink spiral, round gold door/rings, foam and bubbles, Benny foreground near whirlpool, gold $ tokens, visible glowing drain and narrow cyan five-arrow exit slide at bottom. Source screenshot includes a decorative exterior phone border—match the **in-game content**, not a permanent extra phone-shaped frame.\n34\t\n35\t**04 · THROUGH THE FIVE ARROWS** (`04_through_the_five_arrows.png`). From the SAME drain, Benny shoots onto a steep blue water ramp with EXACTLY FIVE glowing white chevrons. Camera behind/above Benny, large foreground character and long descending tunnel perspective. Concentric gold ring pipe, magenta water edges, white foam, $ tokens following left edge. HUD 5/5, $ 1,330.\n36\t\n37\t**05 · FLOW INTO THE CURRENT** (`05_flow_into_the_current.png`). Slide settles seamlessly into a winding horizontal S-shaped current in a perforated magenta metal tube lined with gold ribs and washer nozzles. Benny centered rear view, ribbon of blue water with pink sides, many bubbles and $ coins. HUD 5/5, $ 1,420. Keep forward swimming sensation fast but controllable.\n38\t\n39\t**06 · CREST THE RINSE ARCH** (`06_crest_the_rinse_arch.png`). Current rises into a large sweeping wave arch, crests and curls downward into the next ringed tunnel. Gold dollar coins must sit ON the curve of water; iridescent bubbles, white foam fringes, gold hoops. Rear camera with tilt adapting naturally to pitch. HUD 5/5, $ 1,680.\n40\t\n41\t**07 · DIVE THE WASHER TUBE** (`07_dive_the_washer_tube.png`). Winding flow through the repeating purple perforated tunnel and golden rings. Same blue/pink stream, many gold coins, Benny seen from behind. HUD 5/5, $ 1,940. **Critical transition:** AFTER the shot's visible winding stretch, the physical tube MUST turn into a truly deep, long, unmistakable downward plunge, significantly below Scene 07 entry elevation. Benny travels all the way to the bottom while the third-person camera follows smoothly; gravity/current, walls and gold rings continue. No portal, fade jump, hidden shortcut, teleport, camera cut or discontinuous tube seam. The BOTTOM OF THAT DROP must turn/flare into the real inlet of Scene 08.\n42\t\n43\t**08 · FINAL SPIN CHAMBER** (`08_final_spin_chamber.png`). The low exit of 07 opens through ONE continuous inlet into a larger round pink-gold metallic drum with perforated platforms, side spray spouts pouring water, purple towel on a shelf, round chrome washer door and a winding blue/pink stream. Same water from 07 flows through 08. HUD 5/5, $ 2,040. Rear camera and coins, no art reset.\n44\t\n45\t**09 · RIDE THE FINAL WAVE** (`09_ride_the_final_wave.png`). Inside the SAME final chamber, a strong high wall of blue/pink water rises at left and rolls along the metallic nozzle machinery; camera follows Benny riding toward the platform/towel near the round door. Same scene materials, path and water continuity. HUD 5/5, $ 2,280.\n46\t\n47\t**10 · SLIDE INTO HIDING** (`10_slide_into_hiding.png`). The same stream narrows into a tented opening beneath plush purple towel on perforated gold platform. Benny slides under and hides. Through the round door the **same official cartoon girl** may be visible in the laundry room; she must not see him. Keep original composition, water and close-up towel placement. HUD 5/5, $ 2,500. Physical movement flows into the Scene 11 ending; no 11th gameplay track appears between these.\n48\t\n49\t**11 · SAFELY HOME — THE ACTUAL FINAL END SCREEN** (`11_safely_home_final_victory.png`). The authentic FINAL image. Camera is inside magenta/gold perforated drum; round washer door on the RIGHT is OPEN; the **same official cartoon girl** leans forward with friendly expression, hands on the folded purple towel on perforated platform. Benny remains hidden, safe. Preserve interior colors, chrome door, platform, gold borders, glimmering leftover blue water at bottom, foam/bubbles and victory badge with checkmark and laurels reading `FINAL SPIN COMPLETE`. Top HUD hearts 5/5, $ 2,500, pause, and title bar `11 · SAFELY HOME`. **Only substitute the old girl with the exact new cartoon girl.** No extra stage after 11. Let the player see a clear victory moment and optionally replay.\n50\t\n51\t**Reference scores vs live state:** The cited coin counters are exact values for deterministic screenshot checkpoints. In actual gameplay, counters must change upon real collections. Make the testing/replay seed spawn enough pickups to reach these checkpoints or use a deterministic visual QA state; do NOT fake coin collection by drawing a counter that never responds.\n52\t\n53\t## 3. ART STYLE, WATER & CAMERA — TOP PRIORITY\n54\t\n55\tVisual goal is the same saturated, glossy, ultra-polished **cartoon-3D candy-laundry** style as the references—not generic pastel, blocky low-poly, dark realistic metal, or thin transparent blue puddles. Gold metallic rings must be thick and reflective, magenta perforations visible, washer interior spacious but not empty; appropriately dense pearlescent bubbles, tight character framing, electric cyan core water plus vivid hot-pink flow bands, strong white/frothy edge highlights, and sparkling specular reflections. Keep gold $ coins large, dimensional, lit and anchored to the playable path. Match the typography and UI trim without painting text into the world.\n56\t\n57\t**Water FX Specialist is required:** create a real Claude Code subagent named `water-fx-specialist`, NOT merely claim an official water plugin exists. Build one reusable real-time physically routed spline water system with animated custom Three.js GLSL shaders, adjustable wave heights, UV/advection speed, Fresnel/specular bands, foam edge geometry/particle billboards, caustics/light streaks, spray trails, and transparent iridescent soap bubbles (instancing/LOD where useful). Shape the 03 whirlpool, 04 steep slide, 06 arch, 07 deep plunge, 09 high final wave and 10 towel entry with **actual traversable 3D geometry**. Water direction must match Benny movement and camera speed. If Blender offline fluid sims are used as art aids, bake textures/meshes and optimize them; don't attempt expensive full fluid simulation at runtime. Avoid purple-gray muddy floor, flat opaque ribbon, arbitrary surf foam ring or Benny buried under the surface when he should ride it.\n58\t\n59\t**Camera:** use third-person behind or slightly above Benny on 04–10; his back/hat remains visible with enough forward distance to see coins, currents, turns and hazards. Stage 03 is an intentional dynamic whirlpool angle; Scene 02 is a cinematic tumble; Scene 01 and 11 are inside-drum cinematic angles. On 07→08 descent, pitch and mild roll/turn follow the path smoothly with no abrupt snap. Match approved camera keyframe FOV, horizon, main subject size, washer ring/door positions, and UI safe-area spacing.\n60\t\n61\t## 4. GAMEPLAY ENGINE AND WORLD STRUCTURE\n62\t\n63\tBuild actual playable portrait Android-ready 3D, preferably **Three.js + TypeScript + Vite + GLTF/GLB models**, using **Capacitor** for Android deployment if available; use WebGL compatible mobile shading and build/test scripts. No fullscreen static reference/backdrop/video trick. One connected 3D world with a parameterized continuous route graph/splines; each scene is a checkpoint on a real path, not 11 separate unrelated rooms. Use positions, tangents, curvature, banking, speeds, direction and **absolute altitudes**; validate positional/tangent continuity at every boundary; specifically make 07 end altitude much lower than its start and verify the lower inlet of 08 matches.\n64\t\n65\tControls: a single fast-but-controllable auto-propelled swim/slide current; left/right steer to collect coins, avoid tunnel walls and maintain clear camera; paws paddle, beanie and pom bounce in water; option to pause/resume; 5-heart state; real collectible interactions/counters. Animated girl should blink, hold towel naturally, move at normal pace and not appear robotic/slow-mo. Never jump outside washer into an unrelated world or insert a portal. Ensure fps/memory and loading on Android are measured, not assumed; budget geometry, textures, instancing and bubble counts accordingly.\n66\t\n67\t## 5. 3D ART, TOOLS, INSTALLATION & CREDIT SAFETY\n68\t\n69\tPriority 1: precise manually/procedurally modeled Blender environments—repeatable perforated metal drums, circular gold ring ribs, nozzles, platforms, chrome door, tunnel curvature; UV/material calibration and exact camera/keyframe matching. Export reusable mobile-optimized GLB assets with appropriate PBR. Use **one canonical Benny GLB rig** and **one canonical cartoon girl GLB rig**. Do not use a 2D projection masquerading as a 3D asset.\n70\t\n71\tConnect and VERIFY, only if available and safe, the following (see `TOOL_SETUP_AND_VERIFICATION.md` for official docs and commands):\n72\t- **Blender MCP** to drive the real Blender application, model/texture/rig/refine props, inspect and export GLBs. It is a community tool, not official Blender.\n73\t- **Playwright MCP** to open the actual running browser WebGL game and take real portrait gameplay screenshots, ins